Apple today released watchOS 27.0.1, a minor update to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/watchos-27/">watchOS 27</a> operating system <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/14/apple-releases-watchos-27/">that came out last week</a>. The update is limited to the Apple Watch Series 12 and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-watch-ultra/">Apple Watch Ultra 4</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/watchos-27.jpg" alt="" width="1319" height="742" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1051912" /><br/>
watchOS 27.0.1 can be downloaded through the Settings app on the watch or the Apple Watch app on a connected iPhone. Software can only be installed when the Apple Watch is on the charger and has over 50 percent battery.<br/>
<br/>
